--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**`.
That path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group (the app
targets list `Sources` + `TeslaSync/{widget-primitives,dashboard-widgets,feature-views,
misc-surfaces,shared-surfaces}` — there is no `TeslaSync/Features`). The repo's real,
compiled canonical admin-page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**` — where the
sibling P7 admin pages (ApiPlayground, DiskForecast, SchemaDrift, FleetTelemetryCoverage,
LiveSignalInspector, TeslaOrders) ship and which `Sources` already lists as a project.yml
source path (createIntermediateGroups). The page therefore ships at
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**`, the faithful equivalent of the prompt's
`Features/Admin`. Strings ship in the platform catalog `apps/apple/Localization/
Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the same reconciliation the
DiskForecast / SchemaDrift logs recorded; it is the only deviation from the literal
prompt path.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route is the admin sub-path `/admin/audit-log`. Following the
sibling SchemaDrift/LiveSignalInspector pattern, a dedicated `.auditLog` AppRoute case is
added (pathSegment `audit-log`, System group, icon `list.bullet.rectangle.portrait`),
`AppRouteParser` aliases `/admin/audit-log` → `.auditLog`, and
`AuditLogRouteRegistration` hosts `AuditLogPage` on it, chained into `\.routeHosts` in
TeslaSyncApp.swift. So the page is reachable via the System-group sidebar entry and any
`/admin/audit-log` deep link. (Navigation registration is an allowed file per the prompt.)

