DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI AuditLogPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing the list state
(loading/empty/error/success + the 503 subsystem-unavailable variant) and the hash-chain
verify state (idle/verifying/verified/failed) over an injectable AuditLogDataSource seam whose
value types mirror the web AuditLogRow / AuditChainVerifyResponse 1:1 (production binds the KMP
OperatorConfidenceStore audit endpoints through the seam). The page reproduces the web chrome
(title/subtitle), the subsystem-unavailable AlertBanner, and the three GlassPanels — hash-chain
integrity (Verify-chain action + intact/broken badge + rows-checked/first-bad-row captions),
the eight-filter row (toggle-gated since/until DatePickers, category/action menus fed from the
distinct-value feeds, free-text actor/entity-type, rows-per-page, Reset/Search), and the
paginated entries table with an adaptive layout (columnar Grid on macOS/iPad, per-row cards on
iPhone) covering all eight web columns plus the expandable ExpandedDetail (IP, user-agent,
trace id, before/after JSON, row hash) — using the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (no
hand-rolled glass). Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key
names (50 keys); date/relative/JSON formatting is ported from dateFormat.ts and unit-tested.
Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks (macOS 0/0 + iOS 0/0,
exercising the compact branches) and an executed model harness (all assertions passed). The full
xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due to a pre-existing, out-of-scope swift-frontend crash on the
generated TeslaSync/shared-surfaces mega-codebase (164 out-of-scope files in the crashing batch,
ZERO of mine; forbidden to commit-fix), with ZERO diagnostics in any of my files.

